<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of February 4 in the July-to-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>Additionally, on February 6, the EU granted exports of 211,350 tonnes of soft wheat, 26,000 tonnes of barley, 12,000 tonnes of durum, 2,000 tonnes of oats and 35,000 tonnes of maize. Figures ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			     1Jul96 to 4Feb97	1Jul95 to 4Feb97</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  6,746     150     767    4,499	1,155</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    3,931     114	10    3,453	   13</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		246	65	 -	379	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   98	92	 -	106	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	305	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   13		   -	 76	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   11,034     125     777    8,818	1,168</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	   91		 336	 17	  780</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   292     913	 0	 32	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 68	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     384     328     336	117	  780</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	    11,418     128   1,113    8,935	1,948</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     4,058     326	31    1,244	  128</p>
<p>  Malt (4)	     2,657     121	 0    2,191	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  6,715     195	31    3,435	  128</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	   92   1,840     296	  5	2,268</p>
<p>  Food aid		  11		   -	 11	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL MAIZE	     103     644     296	 16	2,268</p>
<p>  Rye (grain)	    699	56	 3    1,247	   33</p>
<p>  Rye flour (5)	    0		   0	  0	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (5)	    0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL RYE		 699	56	 3    1,247	   33</p>
<p> OATS			375     483	 1	 81	    1</p>
<p>  Sorghum (grain)	  0		   5	  0	  875</p>
<p>  Food aid		   0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SORGHUM	     0		   5	  0	  875</p>
<p>OTHER GRAINS</p>
<p>Buckwheat, Millet,</p>
<p>   Triticale		 1		 147	  1	   86</p>
<p> TOTAL GRAIN	  19,311     141   1,596   13,715	5,339</p>
<p>Note -- (1) column shows this year's exports expressed as a percentage of last year's exports, not as a percentage change (2) wheat equivalent (3) durum equivalent (4) barley equivalent (5) rye equivalent.</p>
